    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "DAY6 — You Were Beautiful",
      "content": "Contradictory simultaneous states. \"Even while laughing, I cry.\"\n\nOne of DAY6's signature songs, built almost entirely around a single repeated word: 예뻤어 — 'you were beautiful,' past tense. The singer is clear upfront that he's not trying to get back together — he's just been hit by a memory and wants to say it out loud once.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-다가도**, which means \"even while in the middle of.\" We'll see how DAY6 uses it in \"You Were Beautiful.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **생각하다** — to think\n- **혼자** — alone\n- **웃다가도 울다** — to cry even while laughing\n- **생각하다가도** — even while thinking\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
